WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.250
Want to try the version one laptop prototype?

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.350
Clone the repo on your laptop.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.200
Connect your microphone to an XLR-to-USB audio interface,
and the interface output to the console.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.300
Install the package.

5
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:20.900
List your devices, pick the input and the output,
then run it in real time.

6
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.050
You'll need a 64-bit laptop running Python 3.10 or newer,

7
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.900
and an interface with at least one XLR mic input
and a line-level output.

8
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.500
For the closed loop, feed a line-level copy
of the speaker feed into a second input.

9
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:44.900
Start at 48 kHz with a 128 to 256 sample callback.

10
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.000
Watch the times that nullyn rt prints,
and raise the block size if you need to.

11
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.600
It's open source, and in active development.

12
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.000
nullyn.ai
